From dc6128fc9ee98f23d64d41ef21e4b6b03a3fd2e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 22:22:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ci: run browser E2E jobs in the official Playwright image

The three browser jobs (Electron E2E, Web Canvas continuity, Web UI E2E)
installed their browsers on every run. Two of them did so with
`playwright install --with-deps`, which goes through apt. That usually
takes 20 to 50 seconds, but one Electron shard spent 13.5 minutes there on
2026-10-26, which looks like a slow mirror. Microsoft's Playwright image
carries the browsers and their system libraries, so all three jobs now run
in it, and the install steps are gone. The disk cleanup goes too: it needs
sudo on the host, which a container job does not have.

The browsers in the image are only found by the Playwright version they
were built for, so the provisioning test now checks that each job's image
tag matches @playwright/test in pnpm-lock.yaml and is pinned by digest.
Electron already starts with --no-sandbox on Linux CI, so running as root
in the container needs no change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
